{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"rampart_earth_broken","model_identifier":"rampart_earth_broken","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# rampart_earth_broken\n\nDamaged state below 40 % HP of `rampart_earth` (Patch 5): a deep bite torn out of the front centre down to half height, the top gone on one side, the front slumped into a spill of earth up to 16 u in front of the foot, stakes broken in the spill and sod hanging over the edge. The ends still stand to at least two thirds of the height so a line still reads as a rampart. Swapped in below 40 % HP and back to the cracked state when repaired above 40 %.\n\n- Footprint: 2 x 2 columns (32 x 32 units, 0.90 x 0.90 m; the notes ask for 1 m, rounded to whole columns), centred on the origin, front (enemy side) faces -Z. Height 71 u (2 m) to the sod.\n- Texture: 256 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material.\n- Cubes: 50, all in `finished`; no hidden state sets.\n- The ends (+X and -X) are flat and full height so chunks placed side by side join into one continuous rampart.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 32 x 71 x 32 centred at the origin (the damaged states keep the same hit box: the damage is visual)\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 71, 2): where a defender stands on top."},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"earth_layer_1_a#6f4f32","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-16,0,-16],"to":[2,12,16],"autouv":0,"color":6,"origin":[-16,0,-16],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[62,54,80,66],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[162,32,194,44],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[80,54,98,66],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[194,32,226,44],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,18,32],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[18,0,36,32],"texture"